# Notices and Credits

mac-visualizer is original work, but several of its algorithms and visual concepts were inspired by other open-source audio-visualization projects. None of the source code from those projects is included in this app — only algorithmic ideas and visual aesthetics, neither of which is protected by copyright.

This file exists to credit those projects and document what inspired what, in the spirit of open-source citizenship.

For third-party material that WAS ported into this app (Metal shader ports and adaptations) together with the full license texts required by those licenses, see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

## Algorithmic inspiration

### `BeatDetector` (Sources/Core/BeatDetector.swift)
Inspired by the adaptive onset-detection algorithm in **[goom2k4](https://github.com/goom-project/goom)** (`plugins/audio/goom2k4/sound_tester.c`). License: LGPL-2.1. Our implementation is clean-room Swift — no source code was copied, only the algorithm concept (aged loudness envelope + adaptive threshold with periodic retuning toward a target onset rate). Tuning constants were adapted to our 0–1 amplitude domain.

### `Delaunay` (Sources/Core/Delaunay.swift)
Standard Bowyer–Watson incremental triangulation, plus straightforward Voronoi-dual computation. Both are well-documented in graphics textbooks and on Wikipedia. No third-party implementation was referenced.

### `MarchingSquares` (Sources/Core/MarchingSquares.swift)
Standard marching-squares iso-line extraction with the "separate" tiebreak for saddle cases. Textbook algorithm. No third-party implementation was referenced.

## Visual aesthetics

### `JoyPlotVisualizer`
Style inspired by Joy Division's *Unknown Pleasures* album cover (1979) and similar visualizations in **[stereoDrift](https://github.com/stereoDrift/stereoDrift.github.io)** (`renderJoyPlotChart`). License: unknown — only the visual concept was used, no JS code.

### `HeightfieldVisualizer`
Visual concept (audio-driven 3D grid mesh) inspired by **[libvisual / Nebulus](https://github.com/Libvisual/libvisual)** (`plugins/actor/nebulus`). License: GPL-2.0. The original was a 16×16 heightfield with a rotating camera. Our implementation is independent Swift + Metal.

### `VoronoiVisualizer`
Visual concept (audio-modulated Voronoi tessellation) inspired by **[stereoDrift](https://github.com/stereoDrift/stereoDrift.github.io)** (`renderVoronoiChart`). The cells/blobs/softCells render-mode split is original to this project. The shape-evolution modes (fixed/cycle/drift/perTrack) are original.

### `LavaLampVisualizer`
Visual concept (audio-driven metaball iso-contours) inspired by **[stereoDrift](https://github.com/stereoDrift/stereoDrift.github.io)** (`lavaLamp` mode, which uses `d3.contourDensity`). Both shader and marching-squares render modes are independent Swift/Metal implementations.

### `IrisVisualizer` and `TricentricVisualizer`
Independent Swift reimplementations inspired by the **Iris** and **Tricentric** presets from **[Vissonance](https://github.com/tariqksoliman/Vissonance)** by Tariq Soliman. License: MIT. The originals are THREE.js/WebGL; our implementations are independent Swift reimplementations of their geometry and audio-response formulas (petal-ring with loudness-driven color and swell; concentric triangle tunnel with loudness-driven roll), adapted to this app's palette system, stereo band split, and CPU vertex-emit pipeline.

