### `PlasmaVisualizer`
Visual concept (demoscene plasma field) inspired by **[libvisual](https://github.com/Libvisual/libvisual)** (`plugins/actor/plazma`). License: GPL-2.0. Our implementation is an independent, clean-room Metal fragment shader (`plasma_fs`) using the standard sum-of-sines plasma formula; no source code was copied.

### `BumpscopeVisualizer`
Visual concept (audio-lit bump-mapped heightfield) inspired by **[libvisual](https://github.com/Libvisual/libvisual)** (`plugins/actor/bumpscope`). License: GPL-2.0. Our implementation is an independent, clean-room Metal fragment shader (`bumpscope_fs`) using standard per-pixel diffuse lighting; no source code was copied.

### Color palettes `viridis` and `plasma` (Sources/Core/ColorPalette.swift)
The `viridis` and `plasma` gradient stops are sampled from matplotlib's colormaps of the same names by Stéfan van der Walt and Nathaniel Smith (**[BIDS/colormap](https://github.com/BIDS/colormap)**). These colormaps are released under CC0 1.0 (public domain); no attribution is legally required. Credited here as a courtesy.

### Spinner, Tri-wing model
The watch-movement styling of the Tri-wing Spinner model (an engraved ring around a visible bearing, jewels in gold settings, blued screws, stepped wings and blue cap jewels) was inspired by the watches of **Richard Paige (RPaige)**, whose Wrocket watch shows a vintage American pocket-watch movement behind a display back. Inspiration only: the shape, geometry, marks and lettering are original to this project, and no artwork, names or designs from those watches are used. Credited with thanks; this credit does not imply endorsement.

## Algorithmic concepts (standard graphics)

The following standard techniques are used and are credited collectively rather than to any specific project: Gaussian metaballs (`exp(-r²·K)` falloff), per-pixel Voronoi cell rendering via nearest-seed search, palette-driven HDR coloring, MPS Gaussian blur for bloom and soft-edge effects, value noise for procedural drift, and standard projection matrices for 3D-tilted grids.

## Network services (lyrics overlay)

The lyrics overlay uses two public network APIs and reads one public web page over HTTPS; no third-party code from any of them is included in this app:

- **[LRCLIB](https://lrclib.net)** — the public lyrics API used to look up time-synced lyrics (no account required).
- **Google Gemini API** (https://ai.google.dev) — used, with the user's own API key, to translate lyric lines.
- **Spotify public track page** (`https://open.spotify.com/track/<id>`) — read once per track per session to get the track's published length, which corrects lyric matching when Spotify reports a shortened length (for example under Crossfade). Only the track id is sent. This is an unofficial read of a public web page, not an official Spotify API; if the page changes, only this length correction is lost.

## Projects we surveyed but did NOT integrate

The following projects were studied during early-stage research (a local collection of audio-visualization repositories). Their algorithms and aesthetic ideas may have influenced our design choices, but no source code from any of them was integrated into this app:

- **[projectM](https://github.com/projectM-visualizer/projectm)** (LGPL-2.1) — MilkDrop reimplementation; considered for direct integration but not pursued.
- **[butterchurn](https://github.com/jberg/butterchurn)** (MIT) — WebGL MilkDrop port; considered as a reference for a future Metal port.
- **[MilkDrop 3](https://github.com/milkdrop2077/MilkDrop3)** (BSD-3) — DirectX-based Windows visualizer; visual reference only.
- **[UnityAudioVisualizer](https://github.com/keijiro/UnityAudioVisualizer)** (Apache-2.0) — HDR particle gradients + wireframe shader algorithm; we wrote independent Metal equivalents.
- **[AudioKit](https://github.com/AudioKit/AudioKit)** (MIT/Apache-2.0) — Swift audio framework; not currently a dependency.
- **[AudioVisualizerKit](https://github.com/AudioVisualizerKit/AudioVisualizerKit)** — FFT + windowing reference; we use vDSP directly.
- **[libvisual](https://github.com/Libvisual/libvisual)** plugins (GPL-2.0) — jakdaw, blursk, oinksie, corona — algorithm and aesthetic survey only. (goom2k4, nebulus, plazma and bumpscope from the same collection also informed specific features and are credited individually above.)
- **[SwiftUI-AudioKit-Visualizer](https://github.com/AudioKit/Cookbook)**, **[AudioPlaybackVisualizer](https://github.com/0xLeif/AudioPlaybackVisualizer)**, **[VisuAc](https://github.com/microcosm/VisuAc)**, **[stereoDrift](https://github.com/stereoDrift/stereoDrift.github.io)**, **[react-native-waveform-player](https://github.com/markusewerth/react-native-waveform-player)**, **[synesthesia](https://github.com/jameswebster/synesthesia)**, **[kaleidosync](https://github.com/zachwinter/kaleidosync)**, **[wavesync](https://github.com/cellofellow/wavesync)** — design and feature survey only.

